Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 01:12:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Phase II Rung 2: scale ice transport to the fiducial grid

Proves the ice-transport generation on the fiducial 16-bin grid with several ice
species, after the small new logic was validated on the 3-bin toy.

- tests/fixture_ice_fiducial/: 16-bin mass-doubling grid (a_min 1e-6, a_max 3.2e-5),
  4 prime elements (H,He,C,O), three inert ice species JCO/JH2O/JCO2 given as base
  totals in abundances.in (exercising the area-weighted IC on a real grid).
- The injector now reports the term-count breakdown; on this fixture:
  120 grain + 675 ice-transport (225 ordered non-overflow pairs x 3 species) = 795.
  Ice transport is O(N^2 N_ice): extrapolating to the reduced network's N_ice ~ tens
  gives ~1e4, the tractable regime the brief requires (not ~1e5).
- tests/coag_ice_scale.sh gates it: total ice sum_k Y(J_k X) conserved to 1.4e-16
  for EACH of the three species independently (transport is per-base, never mixing
  species), and the term count stays < 1e5. PASS.

coag-OFF byte-identical (jac_weight_check 13450, worst reldiff 1.8006e-3).

Rung 2 is complete and locked: ice rides its grains through coagulation with the
corrected encoding (catalyst partner, bare K_ii, ice-follows-particle same-eps),
conserving each species to machine precision, with the initial ice placed
area-weighted by default (or per-species override with a coverage guard). Full gate
set: (a) conservation, dust-mass, ice rate, (b) eps-split hand-check, (d) IC
round-trip+shape+coverage, jacobian weight-plumbing on ice deposits, and fiducial
scaling -- all green, coag-OFF byte-identical throughout.
